<!--
  ============================================================================
  RUT_WelcomeBlanket.xml                 UtinniPatches · COMMISSION_LEDGER_CLEANUP_1
  ============================================================================
  the_scald sheet commission (`ledger:the_scald:welcome-blanket-thermophile-
  mats-rainbow-banded-by-temperatu`, the_scald.md §4 "the welcome blankets"
  and §7 "rainbow pigment"): "rainbow sheets of thermophile bacteria and
  algae coating everything in the depths, oddly fuzzy, banded by
  temperature... the mats at the margins are a pigment source — rainbow
  dyes from the most ancient life there is." the_scald.json new_defs row 3
  flags this "flora authoring, not new species" with mechanic_load
  "injection gating (ban 2: any plant here is wreck-shade-gated)" — that
  ban note is fall_line's, misfiled onto this row in the register; this
  sheet's own real gate is §6 ban 4 ("no macro-life in the boil itself" —
  the mats are bacterial film, not macro-life, so they are unaffected) and
  the "only at the margins" line quoted above, which this def satisfies by
  restricting wild spawn to the `RUT_ScaldMarginMat` terrain tag (added
  this pass to `RUT_ScaldMargin.xml`) rather than the general `Water` tag
  every boil terrain also carries — spawning it on open boil water would
  put a plant on the biome's own "nothing swims/grows the roiling surface"
  ban.

  🔴 maxGrowthTemperature EXPLICITLY OVERRIDDEN to 90 (engine default is 58,
  `PlantProperties.cs:93` in the decompiled source, MEASURED this pass —
  Core ships no XML override on `PlantBaseNonEdible`/`PlantBase`, so every
  plant not touching this field is capped at 58). the_scald.md §0's own
  measured air range is +58..+70 degC (Anvil substellar band) — AT or ABOVE
  that default ceiling — so an unedited plant literally could not grow in
  its own biome's real ambient heat, which would be exactly backwards for
  a def whose whole admission test (§4) is "thrives in heat that kills
  everything else." 90 gives clear headroom above the measured 70 degC
  high without inventing an arbitrary huge number.

  completelyIgnoreFertility + fertilitySensitivity 0: `RUT_ScaldMargin` is
  `ParentName="WaterShallowBase"`, which sets `fertility 0`
  (`PlantUtility.cs:85` requires >=0.9 by default) — same mechanism and
  same citation `RUT_Plant_Wick.xml` (this mod's own aquatic-plant
  precedent, Sump biome) already used and proved.

  No sowTags: this is wild-forage bacterial film, not a player-sown crop —
  the sheet's own text is "coating," "mats," never "cultivated" (contrast
  `RUT_Plant_Wick`, explicitly "grown in station gardens," which does carry
  sowTags). Harvest is direct wild-plant harvesting, which needs no sow
  route.

  harvestedThingDef RUT_RainbowPigment (ThingDefs_Items/, same pass): the
  sheet's own "pigment source — rainbow dyes."

  Placeholder-only art (`Things/Plant/Ambrosia`, same vanilla texPath this
  mod's own `RUT_Plant_Wick.xml` already reuses for an unbuilt aquatic
  plant) — real art queued this pass, `rutwelcomeblanket_v1`
  (`infrastructure/artpipe/pending/`). Checked `infrastructure/artpipe/
  done/`, `pending/`, and `registry.jsonl` by subject first (welcome
  blanket / thermophile mat / rainbow pigment / scald mat) — clean, no
  existing render found.

  Wild only, no player sowing: growDays/harvestYield/harvestWork are this
  pass's own INVENTED-BUILD placeholder values (bacterial-mat scale — fast
  regrowth, small yield per harvest, since the source is "everywhere in the
  depths," not a single crop stand); expect replacement once an items pass
  sets real economy numbers, matching this mod's own stated practice on
  `RUT_WickStem.xml` ("items pass owns pricing").
  ============================================================================
-->
<Defs>

  <ThingDef ParentName="PlantBaseNonEdible">
    <defName>RUT_WelcomeBlanket</defName>
    <label>welcome blanket</label>
    <description>A fuzzy, rainbow-banded sheet of thermophile bacteria and algae, coating the Scald's margins in bands that read the water's own temperature back at you. It is the oldest life on the whole planet, wearing the loudest colors — the shore's one truth that never lies about the heat.</description>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>Things/Plant/Ambrosia</texPath>
      <graphicClass>Graphic_Random</graphicClass>
      <drawSize>0.85</drawSize>
    </graphicData>
    <selectable>true</selectable>
    <pathCost>8</pathCost>
    <statBases>
      <MaxHitPoints>50</MaxHitPoints>
      <Flammability>0</Flammability>
    </statBases>
    <plant>
      <completelyIgnoreFertility>true</completelyIgnoreFertility>
      <fertilitySensitivity>0</fertilitySensitivity>
      <wildTerrainTags>
        <li>RUT_ScaldMarginMat</li>
      </wildTerrainTags>
      <minGrowthTemperature>0</minGrowthTemperature>
      <maxGrowthTemperature>90</maxGrowthTemperature>
      <harvestTag>Standard</harvestTag>
      <harvestedThingDef>RUT_RainbowPigment</harvestedThingDef>
      <harvestYield>4</harvestYield>
      <harvestWork>120</harvestWork>
      <growDays>3</growDays>
      <visualSizeRange>0.5~0.9</visualSizeRange>
      <topWindExposure>0</topWindExposure>
      <wildOrder>2</wildOrder>
      <purpose>Misc</purpose>
    </plant>
  </ThingDef>

</Defs>
